## Plotly: The ggplot2 bridge

:::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="50%"}

- Make a `ggplot2` chart interactive with `ggplotly()`
- Converted legends and tooltips often need cleanup
- Use native `plot_ly()` when interaction is central to the design

```r
library(ggplot2)
library(plotly)

p <- ggplot(iris, aes(
  Sepal.Length, 
  Sepal.Width, 
  colour = Species
)) + 
  geom_point()

ggplotly(p)
```

